{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1572","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1572","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1572\",\"parent_revision\":\"88b183afc7d6ee0af784f20a190f5d5e0757766d445f551b0cc283bd96c73534\",\"root_revision\":\"88b183afc7d6ee0af784f20a190f5d5e0757766d445f551b0cc283bd96c73534\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nProblem: When a SAM task completes or fails, the only audit trail is the session transcript (analyzed post-hoc via kaizen). There is no structured, queryable record of what the agent learned, what questions remained unanswered, what approaches were tried and abandoned, what assumptions were made, or what decisions were taken with their rationale. task_status_hook.py records status transitions and timestamps but not epistemic artifacts. complete-implementation runs quality gates but does not log what was learned.\\n\\nTarget state: The SAM task model (sam_schema/core/models.py) includes optional structured artifact fields on each task record:\\n- findings: list of {fact, source, confidence} dicts logged during implementation\\n- unknowns: list of {question, impact} dicts for unanswered questions at task completion\\n- dead_ends: list of {approach, outcome, lesson} dicts for abandoned approaches\\n- decisions: list of {choice, rationale, alternatives} dicts for implementation decisions\\n\\nThe start-task skill instructs agents to log artifacts via sam_update as they work. The complete-implementation skill summarizes artifacts in quality gate output. Artifacts persist in the SAM task YAML and are queryable via sam_read.\\n\\nHow to verify: Run mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_read(plan=\\\"P{N}\\\", task=\\\"T{M}\\\") on a completed task. The response JSON includes non-empty findings, unknowns, dead_ends, or decisions arrays. At least one artifact type is populated for tasks that involved investigation or debugging.\\n\\nResearch first:\\n? How does Empirica's transaction artifact model handle artifact volume \u2014 are artifacts summarized or raw?\\n? What is the impact on task YAML file size when artifacts are stored inline vs in separate files?\\n? How should agents be prompted to log artifacts without disrupting implementation flow?\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **structured epistemic artifact logging per task (findings, unknowns, dead-ends)** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-infrastructure/empirica.md \u2014 pattern: Epistemic artifact types (Finding, Unknown, Dead-End, Decision, Assumption) logged per transaction\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"1d8cfbb91e7f6efd879ac903b7a40122606f9416efd8796d682df3a0372cc712\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdrwVA\"}"}